import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Lifts
import Lemma.Int.LocalRing.Etale
import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.Etale
open IsLocalRing

/-!
# Monogenicity of finite extensions of discrete valuation rings

Let `A` and `B` be commutative integral domains that are discrete valuation rings, with `B`
a finite local `A`-algebra. If the induced residue-field extension is separable, then `B`
is generated by a single element over `A`.

The proof lifts a primitive element of the residue-field extension and perturbs it by a
multiple of a uniformizer, chosen so that the value of the lifted minimal polynomial is
again a uniformizer (this is where separability is used); Nakayama's lemma then promotes
the resulting approximation to full generation. No unramifiedness is assumed.

## Main results

* `IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_generator_with_residue_minpoly_uniformizer`:
  strengthened monogenicity — the generator comes with a monic lift `F` of the
  residue minimal polynomial whose value is a uniformizer.
* `IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_adjoin_eq_top_of_separable_residueField`: the theorem
  above, allowing ramification (a projection of the strengthened version).
* `IsDiscreteValuationRing.adjoin_eq_top_of_lift_of_map_maximalIdeal`: unramified
  refinement — when the maximal ideal extends to the maximal ideal (ramification index
  one), every lift of a residue-field generator generates `B`.
* `IsDiscreteValuationRing.etale_of_isSeparable_residueField_of_finrank_eq`: residue
  separability plus equality of the extension finrank and residue-field finrank implies
  `Algebra.Etale A B`.

## ATLAS source correspondence for the étale criterion

The final theorem is infrastructure for ATLAS NumberTheoryI N211, Theorem
10.13. At atlas-lean commit `e8b31c5cb0bec89b487ce33fe525a2c0b0f8b9c6`,
the exact theorem is indexed in
[`v1/Atlas/NumberTheoryI/targets.yaml`, lines 1466--1483](https://github.com/facebookresearch/atlas-lean/blob/e8b31c5cb0bec89b487ce33fe525a2c0b0f8b9c6/v1/Atlas/NumberTheoryI/targets.yaml#L1466-L1483):
finite unramified extensions of a complete DVR correspond to finite
separable residue-field extensions. The source encodes an unramified DVR
extension by `LocalExtensions.IsUnramifiedDVRExtension`,
[`v1/Atlas/NumberTheoryI/code/LocalExtensions.lean`, lines 269--273](https://github.com/facebookresearch/atlas-lean/blob/e8b31c5cb0bec89b487ce33fe525a2c0b0f8b9c6/v1/Atlas/NumberTheoryI/code/LocalExtensions.lean#L269-L273).
Its ambient
hypotheses are DVRs `A` and `B`, a finite local algebra map `A → B`; its two
fields are precisely

* separability of `ResidueField B / ResidueField A`, and
* `finrank A B = finrank (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B)`.

Those ambient hypotheses are the section variables below, the first field is
the `Algebra.IsSeparable` instance, and the second is `hfin`.
`etale_of_isSeparable_residueField_of_finrank_eq` proves that this exact source
criterion yields `Algebra.Etale A B`: it obtains a monogenic generator from the
preceding Theorem 10.12 formalization, uses `hfin` to identify the reduction of
its minimal polynomial with the residue minimal polynomial, transports
separability, and applies the local monogenic étale criterion. Completeness is
not used in this implication; N211 needs it elsewhere to construct/lift the
objects, not to turn an already finite local DVR extension satisfying these two
unramified conditions into an étale algebra.
-/


namespace IsDiscreteValuationRing

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
  [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [IsDiscreteValuationRing B]
  [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]

end IsDiscreteValuationRing
